# docs-geode is Teacher at the Door

**Seated:** `20261107.211138` on Keaton's word - **Status:** Living
**Molted from:** [`docs-geode-bhakta`](docs-geode-bhakta.mdc) (W2, checkpoint `20261107.211138`)
**Kin:** [`teacher-style`](teacher-style.mdc) - [`bhakta-style`](bhakta-style.mdc) - [`radiant-style`](radiant-style.mdc) - [`gauge-style`](gauge-style.mdc)

`docs-geode/` is the shelf a person reads in order to learn the product. Its register is **Teacher Style**: the secular open door, same moves as Bhakta in plain American English. Gauge remains the working style of the rest of the tree. Inside this folder, Gauge is the measurement dial, and the dial stays at **Door**.

## What every page declares

Every Markdown page under `docs-geode/`, drafts in `edu/yonder/` included, carries one style line:

`**Style:** Teacher at the Door setting, with Radiant warmth`

The line points at `context/TEACHER_STYLE.md`. It names Teacher and Door. It does not name Gauge as the page's register.

A page written by a generator declares the same line in the generator, so the next render keeps it. `tools/fixtures/g/geode_libraries_scan.sh` is the library index's source.

## What the next edit of a body does

Teacher's moves govern the prose from here forward. One new idea at a time. A coined word is given in plain speech the first time it appears. Why the thing matters to a life is said once. A figure still carries its unit, its date, and its source, which is the Gauge measurement Teacher keeps.

## What holds it

```
sh tools/fixtures/d/docs_geode_teacher_scan.sh
rishi/bin/rishi run tools/d/docs_geode_teacher_witness.rish
```

The scan reads every `*.md` under `docs-geode/`. A page with no style line, a style line without Teacher, or a style line that names Gauge, is a miss. `verdict=ok` means the folder's doors agree.

